      "message": "Done.\n\n\u003e Note also that one painful lesson that I learned is that the context object passed to settings is only used the first time and stashed in a static thereafter.\n\nYes the whole point of this refactor to the captive portal settings is to never call Settings.Global.getFoo() in the tests at all, because stateful static functions are evil.",
